  <section class="coc-section coc-dark" aria-labelledby="coc-intro-title">
    <div class="coc-wrap">
      <span class="coc-eyebrow">Our Commitment</span>
      <h2 class="coc-heading" id="coc-intro-title">Development Beyond the Field</h2>
      <p class="coc-copy">At Fayetteville Fury, development is about more than what happens on the field. Our Code of Conduct establishes the standards we expect from players, parents, coaches, staff, and everyone who represents Fury. It is designed to create an environment where players can develop, compete, learn from mistakes, build confidence, and support one another.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="coc-primary" aria-label="Download the complete Code of Conduct">
    <div class="coc-wrap coc-primary-inner">
      <div><span class="coc-eyebrow">Complete Policy</span><p class="coc-copy">The PDF is the authoritative complete version of the Fayetteville Fury Code of Conduct, Revised 2026.</p></div>
      <a class="coc-button" href="Fury Code of Conduct.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Download the Full Code of Conduct</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="coc-section" aria-labelledby="coc-covers-title">
    <div class="coc-wrap">
      <span class="coc-eyebrow">The Standard</span>
      <h2 class="coc-heading" id="coc-covers-title">What the Code Covers</h2>
      <div class="coc-grid">
        <article class="coc-card"><h3 class="coc-card-title">Respect</h3><p class="coc-card-copy">Treat players, coaches, parents, officials, opponents, volunteers, and staff with dignity and respect. Differences should never become a reason to criticize, isolate, embarrass, intimidate, or diminish another person.</p></article>
        <article class="coc-card"><h3 class="coc-card-title">Player Development &amp; Team Culture</h3><p class="coc-card-copy">Players develop at different rates. Fury expects teammates to encourage one another, communicate constructively, accept coaching, and understand that mistakes are part of development.</p></article>
        <article class="coc-card"><h3 class="coc-card-title">Sportsmanship</h3><p class="coc-card-copy">Players, coaches, and families should respect teammates, opponents, officials, coaches, spectators, and tournament personnel. Winning should never come at the expense of integrity, respect, or development.</p></article>
        <article class="coc-card"><h3 class="coc-card-title">Anti-Bullying</h3><p class="coc-card-copy">Bullying, harassment, intimidation, deliberate exclusion, repeated belittling, threats, and conduct intended to demean or negatively target another player are inconsistent with Fury values.</p></article>
        <article class="coc-card"><h3 class="coc-card-title">Accountability</h3><p class="coc-card-copy">Accountability means acknowledging mistakes, learning from them, taking appropriate corrective action, and continuing to improve.</p></article>
        <article class="coc-card"><h3 class="coc-card-title">Player Safety &amp; Welfare</h3><p class="coc-card-copy">Players should be able to learn, compete, make mistakes, ask questions, and grow without fear of humiliation, harassment, or intimidation.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="coc-section coc-dark coc-expectations" aria-labelledby="coc-expectations-title">
    <div class="coc-wrap">
      <span class="coc-eyebrow">Shared Responsibility</span>
      <h2 class="coc-heading" id="coc-expectations-title">Expectations</h2>
      <div class="coc-grid">
        <article class="coc-card"><h3 class="coc-card-title">Players</h3><p class="coc-card-copy">Give their best effort, listen to coaches, respect teammates, opponents, and officials, communicate positively, accept responsibility, encourage teammates, learn from mistakes, and represent Fayetteville Fury with pride.</p></article>
        <article class="coc-card"><h3 class="coc-card-title">Parents &amp; Guardians</h3><p class="coc-card-copy">Encourage their child without criticizing others, speak respectfully, reinforce sportsmanship and accountability, use appropriate club channels for concerns, respect family privacy, and model appropriate sideline behavior.</p></article>
        <article class="coc-card"><h3 class="coc-card-title">Coaches</h3><p class="coc-card-copy">Create a positive developmental environment, establish and reinforce conduct expectations, correct inappropriate behavior, provide constructive feedback, communicate with parents appropriately, protect confidentiality, and escalate serious or recurring concerns.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="coc-section" aria-labelledby="coc-accountability-title">
    <div class="coc-wrap">
      <span class="coc-eyebrow">Education and Correction</span>
      <h2 class="coc-heading" id="coc-accountability-title">Accountability</h2>
      <p class="coc-copy">For most situations involving bullying or repeated inappropriate teammate conduct, Fury uses a progressive response intended to provide an opportunity for education and behavioral correction.</p>
      <div class="coc-steps">
        <div class="coc-step"><span class="coc-step-number">First Incident</span><p>Team reminder and parent communication.</p></div>
        <div class="coc-step"><span class="coc-step-number">Second Incident</span><p>Player and parent conference and one-game suspension.</p></div>
        <div class="coc-step"><span class="coc-step-number">Third Incident</span><p>Potential removal from the roster.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="coc-alert">The progressive process does not require every situation to pass through three separate incidents. Serious conduct or a significant concern for another player's safety or well-being may result in immediate suspension or removal from the program when circumstances warrant.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="coc-section coc-dark" aria-label="Reporting concerns and player welfare">
    <div class="coc-wrap coc-split">
      <article class="coc-panel"><span class="coc-eyebrow">Speak Up Early</span><h2 class="coc-heading">Reporting a Concern</h2><p class="coc-copy">Players and parents are encouraged to raise concerns before situations escalate. Concerns may initially be brought to the player's coach. When a concern involves the coach, cannot reasonably be addressed by the coach, involves serious misconduct, or remains unresolved, it may be elevated to the Coaching Director or appropriate Fury leadership.</p></article>
      <article class="coc-panel"><span class="coc-eyebrow">Players First</span><h2 class="coc-heading">Player Welfare</h2><p class="coc-copy">The physical and emotional well-being of our players is a priority. Fayetteville Fury expects adults within the organization to place player welfare ahead of competitive results.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="coc-statement" aria-label="Fayetteville Fury team standard"><div class="coc-wrap"><p>We are one team.<span>We compete at a higher level when we lift each other up.</span></p></div></section>

